title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "true_around"
---
The true border goes into the charter, and the new road goes around the mill, the long way, the old way.
Bram's wheel turns all summer. The steward's carts curse the corner, and take it anyway.
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "true_through"
---
The true border goes into the charter. But the road goes straight, as the steward wanted, and the mill is in its way.
Bram grinds his last sack at midsummer and gives the millstones to the chapel.
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "forged"
---
The steward's border goes into the charter. The abbey loses its meadows, and nobody can say quite why.
<<if $offer == Offer.Accepted>>
    You leave the valley with forty crowns and a map you will never show anyone.
<<else>>
    Corvin bows to you as he passes. It is not a friendly bow.
<<endif>>
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "exposed"
---
By evening the steward is two valleys away, and the true border is in the charter.
The Countess asks you to stay on as the valley's cartographer. The abbey sends a cheese.
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "walked"
---
The border follows the path the village walks, stone to stone. Nobody is pleased, and nobody fights.
Every spring after, the children of Ashcombe and the novices of the abbey walk it together, and argue all the way.
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "failed"
---
The hearing breaks up without a border. The valley goes home and keeps the quarrel for another generation.
You fold the map with its holes and take the road over the hill.
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Accounts
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
---
// What is left of every quest, whatever the ending. Jory's line is a line group: one of the lines that fit.
<<if $quest_border == QuestState.Active>>
    <<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed border>>
<<endif>>
=> Jory dances at the fair on his crutch, and his mother doesn't let go of his sleeve all day. <<if $jory_found>>
=> Jory buys the first cider of the fair for the whole camp, and the camp drinks it twice. <<if $jory_found>>
=> Under the hill, Gudrun's miners are still digging for Jory. They say they hear him singing. <<if not $jory_found>>
=> Nobody under the hill says Jory's name aloud, in case the hill hears. <<if not $jory_found>>
<<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Hedda's fair cake, from her mother's recipe, is gone before noon.
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_lio_map == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Lio's first map hangs behind Hedda's bar, framed, with the old line in red.
<<endif>>
<<if $feast_served>>
    The cook of Varne castle still talks about the feast.
<<endif>>
<<if $pell_trust >= 1>>
    Pell's cart goes over the hill with your story painted on its side.
<<endif>>
<<if $echo_answered>>
    The echo of the deep level never asks another riddle.
<<endif>>
<<ending {$outcome}>>
===
